        "id": "act_rage_7rzi",
        "name": "Rage",
        "actionType": "trait",
        "descriptionHtml": "<p>The lupine can give itself Advantage on its first D20 Test each turn. If it does so and fails that D20 Test, it's overcome with rage. On each of its turns while raging, the lupine attacks the nearest creature it can see. If no creature is near enough to move to and attack, its rage ends. A lupine's ally, if within 60 feet of the raging lupine, can try to calm it by taking an action to make a DC 15 Charisma (Persuasion) check; the lupine must be able to hear its ally. If this check succeeds, the lupine ceases its rage.</p>",
        "entries": [
          "The lupine can give itself {@variantrule Advantage|XPHB} on its first {@dice D20} Test each turn. If it does so and fails that {@dice D20} Test, it's overcome with rage. On each of its turns while raging, the lupine attacks the nearest creature it can see. If no creature is near enough to move to and attack, its rage ends. A lupine's ally, if within 60 feet of the raging lupine, can try to calm it by taking an action to make a {@dc 15} Charisma ({@skill Persuasion|XPHB}) check; the lupine must be able to hear its ally. If this check succeeds, the lupine ceases its rage."
        ],
